{
  "requirement": "Listing and reading failures return errors, distinct from successful empty\nlistings and successful reads of empty files.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.errors`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. A listing failure returns an error.\n2. A read failure returns an error.\n3. A successful empty listing is a success, not an error.\n4. A successful read of an empty file is a success, not an error.\n\n**Failures return errors (obligations 1 and 2)**\n- `failed_provider_operations_never_become_successful_empty_results` uses `FailingProvider`, whose `list` fails or whose `read` fails. In both modes it asserts that `search_text`, `parse` and `search_structure` return an `Err` with the specific message (\"listing failed\" or \"reading failed\"). A failure that was swallowed into an empty result would break these assertions.\n- `completeness_is_false_only_when_a_match_is_omitted_and_errors_propagate` checks that an invalid pattern gives an error. It also checks that invalid UTF-8 and an unknown language make `parse_snapshot` fail.\n- The real filesystem provider is covered in `source_defaults.rs`:\n  - `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` checks that listing a missing scope or a missing root is an error, and that listing a root that is a file is an error. It also checks that reading a missing file, a `../` path or an absolute path is an error.\n  - `scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors` checks that a broken `.gitignore` in a relevant directory makes `list` and `read` fail. On unix it also checks that a symlink makes `list` fail.\n\n**Successes that are empty are not errors (obligations 3 and 4)**\n- `successful_empty_listing_and_empty_resources_are_distinct_from_errors` runs with both an empty and a non-empty listing. It asserts that `list` succeeds, that `read` and `parse` of empty content succeed with empty bytes, and that `search_text` and `search_structure` return `Ok` with `complete` true and no matches.\n- `empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct` asserts that an empty directory lists successfully and that an empty file reads successfully with empty bytes. It does this next to the error cases above, so the success/error distinction is enforced in one place.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found none. The tests cover both operations, both outcomes, and both an in-memory and a filesystem provider. All the tests carry `{test}` references to the requirement, and no `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "4b9203b0a488dc4487cc9c5b785258007920be5ad703e2cd52ebadf5d9e380bc",
